Drag the caret by pressing on it, and keep the magnifier below the shell bar.

On a phone people press the caret itself and drag it, as in any HarmonyOS
text field; Chromium only takes the handle below it, and touches on the
text line above the handle deliberately fall through. On OHOS, for the
insertion handle only, a touch on the caret line within a touch radius
counts as a touch on the handle, so pressing the caret and dragging moves
it, and tapping it toggles the menu. Selection handles are unchanged.

The magnifier sits above the caret and is kept inside its parent layer,
which was the root window's, whose top is under the shell's status and
address bars; near the top of a page it slid under them. On OHOS it is
parented to the page's own layer, which begins below the bars.

Generated against Chromium 154.0.8037.51 with chromium-154-harmonyos.patch
and ohos-touch-menu-below-shell-bar.patch applied. Apply with:
  git apply ohos-touch-caret-drag.patch

